SUMMARY:St. Agnes Christmas & Craft Bazaar
DESCRIPTION:The St. Agnes Christmas & Craft Bazaar is an annual event held the first Friday and Saturday in November. We begin the weekend with 8:00 am Mass on Friday – everyone is welcome! Bazaar hours are Friday from 9:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. and Saturday from 9:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.\nThe bazaar is held at St. Agnes Parish Hall, LOWER LEVEL, 1008 McLary Road, Nashville, IN.  Admission and parking are free, and it is elevator accessible.\nSelect from handcrafted Christmas decorations and gifts, handmade wreaths, home baked goods, paper and wood crafts, and decorated tabletop Christmas trees. There is also a silent auction with themed gift baskets and a handmade quilt raffle*.\nProceeds from this year’s Bazaar will benefit Habitat for Humanity, Mother’s Cupboard and St. Vincent de Paul of Brown County.\n*Charity Gaming: (CG License #10834)\n
