SUMMARY:Author Conversation with Kristy Woodson Harvey
DESCRIPTION:Join Naughty Dog Books in conversation with New York Times, USA Today, and Publishers Weekly bestselling author, Kristy Woodson Harvey, as she promotes her latest book, Falling for Peachtree Bluff.\nTicket includes:\nEntry into the event\nA signed hardback copy of Falling for Peachtree Bluff\n(Additional hardback copies and backlist titles will be available for purchase at the event, as supplies last.)\n \nDoors open 30 minutes before the event begins. The evening will consist of one hour of moderated author conversation and Q&A, with an optional meet-and-greet to follow.\n \nAbout the book:\nWelcome to Peachtree Bluff: a cozy coastal town where family secrets refuse to be washed away by the tide and close-knit community is everything. As New York Times bestselling author Kristy Woodson Harvey reunites the Murphy crew just in time for pumpkin spice season, “we dare you not to wish you were a member of this family” (E!).\nEldest sister Caroline has never been happier. The family business is thriving, her kids are great, and her sister Emerson’s hunky costar has absolutely swept her off her feet. But when her not-quite-ex-husband decides it’s high time he begged Caroline for a second chance, she is thrown into the midst of a love triangle she never saw coming. Caroline is the family fixer and, when her sisters Sloane and Emerson and daughter Vivi need her help with their troubles, she has to decide whether to swoop in and save them—or if it’s finally time to focus on what she wants.\nMatriarch Ansley and her new husband, Jack, have finally hit their stride. But when a scandal rips through Peachtree Bluff—and Jack just might be at the center of it—Ansley is left questioning whether the man she has loved since she was sixteen years old, the man she fought so hard to be with, is actually who she thought he was at all.\nThe air is crisper, the water is calmer, but, when it comes to the Murphy family, nothing is ever quite as simple as it seems… Through it all, these Southern women must rely on their powerful family bonds and the quirky characters and small-town charm of the place that, no matter what, always calls them home. This is the kind of heartfelt fall treat that “readers will unwrap with glee” (Mary Kay Andrews, New York Times bestselling author) from the “go-to for elevated beach reads” (People).\n
URL:https://browncounty.com/events/author-conversation-with-kristy-woodson-harvey/
ORGANIZER;CN=Naughty Dog Books:MAILTO:
CATEGORIES:Happening,Literary,Special Events
LOCATION:2359 Indiana 46 E, Nashville, IN
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://browncounty.com/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/naughtydogbooks-Instagram-3715-ig-17917344320725017.jpg
